{"tool_name":"graditude","contents":["oeb","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"graditude","home":"https://foerstner-lab.github.io/GRADitude/","license":"ISC","summary":"GRADitude: a computational tool for Grad-seq data analysis\n\nGrad-seq is a high-throughput profiling approach for the organism-wide detection of RNA-RNA and RNA-protein interactions in which molecular complexes are separated in a gradient by shape and size (Smirnov et al., 2016, PNAS). Grad-seq separates native cellular lysates including complexes, according to their molecular weight and shape in a glycerol gradient, independent of charge and sequence. After this fractionation, RNA-seq and MS-analysis of each of the fractions generated allows the reconstruction of the sedimentation profiles of all detectable RNAs and protein in a single experiment. Further analysis can reveal possible interactions between the individual molecules.","addition_date":"2021-10-14T10:06:39.012130Z","last_update_date":"2022-12-01T20:29:00.992851Z","biotools_curie":"biotools:graditude","documentation":[{"type":["Governance"],"url":"https://foerstner-lab.github.io/GRADitude/"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"name":"GRADitude","owner":"konrad","topic":[{"term":"Molecular biology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3047"},{"term":"RNA-Seq","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3170"}]},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:graditude/undefined/foerstner-lab.github.io","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"binaries":{"freeness":null,"registration":null},"packages":null,"source_packages":true,"sourcecode":{"free":true,"interpreted":true,"license":true,"public":true,"readme":true,"repository":{"anonymous":true,"online":true}}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"license":{"open_source":true,"osi":true},"publications":[],"readme":true,"summary":{"description":true},"website":{"